===Adjective===
{{en-adj|?}}

# Of, to, [[pertaining]] to{{,}} or used for purposes of [[conduct]]ing [[trade]], [[commerce]], [[governance]], [[advocacy]] or other professional purposes.
#: {{ux|en|Please do not use this phone for personal calls; it is a '''business''' phone.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1897|author=Reform Club (New York, N.Y.) Sound Currency Committee|journal=Sound Currency|volume=4-5|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=STIJAQAAIAAJ&hl=en&ei=FaaETYaAJsKdccfR-Z4D&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=15&ved=0CHAQ6AEwDg|page=cclii|passage=They are solely '''business''' instruments. Every man's relation to them is purely a '''business''' relation. His use of them is purely a '''business''' use.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=10|passage=With a little manœuvring they contrived to meet on the doorstep which was {{...}} in a boiling stream of passers-by, hurrying '''business''' people speeding past in a flurry of fumes and dust in the bright haze.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1996|author=Lawyers Co-operative Publishing Company|journal=American Law Reports: Annotations and Cases|volume=35|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=tjI2AQAAIAAJ&q=%22solely+business%22&hl=en&ei=FaaETYaAJsKdccfR-Z4D&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=20&ved=0CIoBEOgBMBM|page=432|passage={{...}} the fact that the injured party came to the insured premises for solely '''business''' purposes precluded any reliance on the non-business pursuits exception (§ 1 1 2[b]).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Marvin Snider|title=Compatibility Breeds Success: How to Manage Your Relationship with Your Business Partner|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=VWeWiBsYm8YC&pg=PA298&hl=en&ei=FaaETYaAJsKdccfR-Z4D&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=18&ved=0CH4Q6AEwEQ#v=onepage&q=%22in%20solely%20business%20partnerships%22&f=false|page=298|passage=Both of these partnerships have to cope with these dual issues in a more complicated way than is the case in solely '''business''' partnerships.}}
# [[professional|Professional]], [[businesslike]], having concern for good business practice.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1889|journal=The Clothier and furnisher|volume=19|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=GSAAAAAAMAAJ&q=%22he+is+thoroughly+business%22&dq=%22he+is+thoroughly+business%22&hl=en&ei=3XuETd7DN8rMcJnpzYUD&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CCkQ6AEwAA|page=38|passage=He is thoroughly '''business''', but has the happy faculty of transacting it in a genial and courteous manner.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1909|publisher=La Salle Extension University|title=Business Administration: Business Practice|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=6lfPAAAAMAAJ&q=%22thoroughly+business+manner%22&dq=%22thoroughly+business+manner%22&hl=en&ei=OHmETb_-O4TCccK9yJcD&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CCsQ6AEwAA|page=77|passage={{...}} and the transaction carried through in a thoroughly '''business''' manner.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1927|title=Making of America Project|journal=w:Harper's Magazine|volume=154|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=SRcwAAAAMAAJ&q=%22very+subtle+contrast+becomes%22&hl=en&ei=2cCETaXcBsKPcaH-5YAD&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=58&ved=0CJYCEOgBMDk4ZA|page=502|passage=Sometimes this very subtle contrast becomes only too visible, as when in wartime Jewish business men were almost lynched because they were thoroughly '''business''' men and worked for profit.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=w:Frank Channing Haddock|title=Business Power: Supreme Business Laws and Maxims that Win Wealth|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=0LY9rKvgsNAC&pg=PA231&dq=%22investigated+them+in+a+thoroughly+business+manner%22&hl=en&ei=P42ETfXYOoj0cYmL0YwD&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CDIQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=%22investigated%20them%20in%20a%20thoroughly%20business%20manner%22&f=false|page=231|passage=The moral is evident: do not invest in schemes promising enormous and quick returns unless you have investigated them in a thoroughly '''business''' manner.}}
# Supporting business, [[conducive]] to the [[conduct]] of business.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1867|editor=w:Edmund Hodgson Yates|title=Amiens|journal=Tinsley's Magazine|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=mWAEAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA430&dq=%22Amiens+is+a+thoroughly+business+town,+the+business+being+chiefly+with+the+flax-+works.%22&hl=en&ei=RpiETcX8O8iecPbwrIwD&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CCkQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=%22Amiens%20is%20a%20thoroughly%20business%20town%2C%20the%20business%20being%20chiefly%20with%20the%20flax-%20works.%22&f=false|page=430|passage=Amiens is a thoroughly '''business''' town, the business being chiefly with the flax-works.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-08|volume=407|issue=8839|page=55|magazine=w:The Economist
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/business/21579011-president-proposes-new-round-intellectual-property-reform-obama-goes-troll-hunting Obama goes troll-hunting]
|passage=According to this saga of intellectual-property misanthropy, these creatures [patent trolls] roam the '''business''' world, buying up patents and then using them to demand extravagant payouts from companies they accuse of infringing them. Often, their victims pay up rather than face the costs of a legal battle.}}

